{"packet":0,"rowIndex":356,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":362,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,363]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:362:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D7"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/41/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/41/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=3]Right? This idea really echos with the idea of time as a whole."}}
{"packet":0,"rowIndex":357,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":363,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,364]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:363:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D7"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/42/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/42/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=1]Though we see time as a day to day thing, thousands of years ago, or thousands of years from now - so many things change, yet so much remains the same."}}
{"packet":0,"rowIndex":358,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":364,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,365]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:364:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D7"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/43/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/43/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=4]A journey without an end - yet time marches on, and flows like a river."}}
{"packet":0,"rowIndex":359,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":365,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,366]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:365:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D7"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/44/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/44/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=5]It’s interesting to consider though, if \"time\" is the \"river,\" then we are the \"water.\""}}
{"packet":0,"rowIndex":360,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":366,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,354]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:366:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D7"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/45/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/45/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=4]And does the \"water\" come back in the form of \"rain\" and \"snow\"?"}}
{"packet":0,"rowIndex":361,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":369,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,370]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:369:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D7"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/48/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/48/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=4]It’s not my greatest one. But I’ve captured a few concepts in this."}}
{"packet":0,"rowIndex":362,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":370,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,371]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:370:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D7"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/49/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/49/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=1]See Rascal, a difficult part of traditional haiku is the split of two ideas."}}
{"packet":0,"rowIndex":363,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":371,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,372]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:371:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D7"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/50/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/50/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=1]Two ideas that contrast each other, they vibrate against each other and change the context of each other."}}
{"packet":0,"rowIndex":364,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":372,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,373]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:372:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D7"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/51/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/51/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=4]The poem is meant to capture both, the phenomena of an instant of observing water, yet the realization that every droplet of water is new."}}
{"packet":0,"rowIndex":365,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":373,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,375]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:373:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D7"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/52/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/52/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=2]Each droplet that passes this place came from a glacier up above, and who knows, maybe it has made its way back here before."}}
